{
 "comment": [
  "nuBuilder Next documentation (English), shown at index.php?p=help – never link the files directly.",
  "One file per page in docs/pages/. Chapters and pages are listed here in reading order; pages/nuhelp.php joins them per tab",
  "(guide = tab Guide, ref = tab Code reference) and numbers them (1, 1.1 …) after filtering, so numbers are never written in the files.",
  "Every file holds exactly one <section id=…> with one <h2 id=…>; sub-sections are <div class=\"doc-sub\"> with an <h3 id=…>.",
  "Ids are anchors (index.php?p=help#id) and must be unique over all files – links from code, the tutorial and other pages use them.",
  "Who sees what (filtered on the server): data-doc=\"admin\" globeadmin and admin roles; data-doc=\"dev\" globeadmin in developer mode;",
  "data-acl=\"nuuser,…\" users with the view right on one of these forms; no attribute = everybody. Works on any element.",
  "A chapter's section must not be more restrictive than its pages (a reader would see pages without their chapter).",
  "Page template: h2, p.doc-lead (purpose and scope), p.doc-for (audience, admin only), content, p.doc-see, details.doc-src (admin only).",
  "data-level=\"advanced\" on a section (or doc-sub) marks an advanced topic: hidden while the reader has \"Show advanced topics\" off (nuhelp.js).",
  "No version numbers in the text – the change history is CHANGELOG.md.",
  "Function references: <div data-nu-fnref=\"tabs\"></div> is replaced with docs/nunext-functions.json (core/nufnref.php)."
 ],
